  "id": "pandavani",
  "name": "Pandavani (Chhattisgarhi Mahabharata ballad)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Pandavani is the sung and acted telling of the Mahabharata story of the Pandava brothers, with Bhima as its hero, in Chhattisgarh. The lead performer holds a tambura, used as a prop as well as a drone, and sings, speaks and acts out the episodes, while a seated group of harmonium, tabla, dholak and manjira players answers, one of them as the ragi who responds to the narrator. It has two styles, the seated vedamati and the theatrical kapalik, the style of Teejan Bai.",
